ypeScript + React First#Dev instruction requirements for UI#{5}":[158,159],"#Architect Agent#Rules":[160,165],"#Architect Agent#Rules#{1}":[161,161],"#Architect Agent#Rules#{2}":[162,162],"#Architect Agent#Rules#{3}":[163,163],"#Architect Agent#Rules#{4}":[164,165]},"outlinks":[],"metadata":{"name":"architect","description":"Senior ServiceNow Technical Architect that converts rm_stories into a full technical design (tables, business rules, flows, client scripts, ACLs, integrations, UIB/React UI specs), a step-by-step dev instruction set in build order, and a test plan traced to acceptance criteria. Use when a solution needs to be planned before anyone builds it: 'design the solution for X', 'what components/tables do we need for Y', 'plan this feature', or when a test/governance failure is a design flaw that needs re-architecting. Not for turning raw requirements into stories (ba-agent) or actually building in ServiceNow (developer).","color":"blue"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[46,68],[74,90],[94,106],[142,150]],"key":"ClaudeAgents/architect.md"},
